{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_0172sbV8xVUyJ4axr4RCq84o","input":{"command":"git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nopencode: fix fabrication against 1.18.5, spec it, test it\n\nThe adapter was written against an inferred format and only ever exercised\non the happy path, so it failed on any conversation containing a tool call —\nwhich is nearly all of them. Verified against opencode 1.18.5.\n\nFormat fixes:\n- tool `state` requires all six of status/input/output/title/metadata/time;\n  omitting any one fails the whole import with `Missing key at [\"state\"][…]`.\n  Only the first three were written, so every tool-bearing bridge died.\n- Pair tool_use with its tool_result up front and carry the real recorded\n  output in `state.output` instead of a placeholder, rather than discarding\n  it and re-emitting the same text loosely alongside the call.\n- Backdate the import notice ahead of history. opencode orders messages by\n  `time.created`, so a notice stamped at fabrication time sorted *after*\n  every turn and rendered with a QUEUED badge, reading as a pending prompt.\n- parentID is a prompt→replies tree, not a linked list: user messages are\n  unparented, assistant messages point at the user message that prompted\n  them. Chaining every message to its predecessor parented user messages to\n  assistant ones.\n- Look `info.projectID` up via `opencode debug scrap` instead of hardcoding\n  the \"global\" project, which listed bridged sessions from every directory.\n- Propagate the source model id per the fabrication contract instead of\n  substituting a fixed fake one.\n- Honor `opts.replayReasoning`, which was ignored: thinking blocks always\n  became native reasoning parts. Off, they fold to labeled text.\n\nRobustness:\n- Import is not atomic — a rejected payload leaves a truncated session in the\n  DB. Delete it, and raise FabricationUnsupportedError so resume falls back to\n  bootstrap instead of surfacing a raw throw.\n- Record lineage against the id opencode actually stored.\n\nRemove the opencode shim. It triggered on `$# -eq 2`, so it intercepted\n`opencode -s <id>`, discarded the id, and re-entered itself through PATH —\nan infinite loop — while the bare form it documented passed through. opencode\nhas no argument-free \"show me my sessions\" invocation to interpose on.\n\nAlso: docs/specs/opencode-session-format.md with the evidence and the\nunknowns, an opencode row in the drift check (`opencode-ai`), opencode in the\ninteractive smoke test (which deletes its own session, since fabrication\nmutates a shared DB), and payload-shape tests covering each defect above.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RSV6y7vfeVapvuhimD3XmQ\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -2","description":"Commit the fixes"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"fix/opencode-adapter","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge/.claude/worktrees/opencode-fixes","dirty_fingerprint":"cf8b9e3c1e47cd671f179e23127d98edb70689fbf4ed08f9960baec974f11cfc","head":"0255ff65551f4f4db35093759cbfc582810818f1","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:f6bb2ded-a3cb-4342-afd7-bbadf34f59ee","seq":462},"id":"ev1-4068b4e6f699df689247d421716e39e221e06f070d20b1e9ef7a998b4f9c6818","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-03T01:13:34.190Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"f6bb2ded-a3cb-4342-afd7-bbadf34f59ee","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.220","tool":"cledger","version":"0.16.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge/.claude/worktrees/opencode-fixes","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"fix/opencode-adapter","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_0172sbV8xVUyJ4axr4RCq84o","input":{"command":"git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nopencode: fix fabrication against 1.18.5, spec it, test it\n\nThe adapter was written against an inferred format and only ever exercised\non the happy path, so it failed on any conversation containing a tool call —\nwhich is nearly all of them. Verified against opencode 1.18.5.\n\nFormat fixes:\n- tool `state` requires all six of status/input/output/title/metadata/time;\n  omitting any one fails the whole import with `Missing key at [\"state\"][…]`.\n  Only the first three were written, so every tool-bearing bridge died.\n- Pair tool_use with its tool_result up front and carry the real recorded\n  output in `state.output` instead of a placeholder, rather than discarding\n  it and re-emitting the same text loosely alongside the call.\n- Backdate the import notice ahead of history. opencode orders messages by\n  `time.created`, so a notice stamped at fabrication time sorted *after*\n  every turn and rendered with a QUEUED badge, reading as a pending prompt.\n- parentID is a prompt→replies tree, not a linked list: user messages are\n  unparented, assistant messages point at the user message that prompted\n  them. Chaining every message to its predecessor parented user messages to\n  assistant ones.\n- Look `info.projectID` up via `opencode debug scrap` instead of hardcoding\n  the \"global\" project, which listed bridged sessions from every directory.\n- Propagate the source model id per the fabrication contract instead of\n  substituting a fixed fake one.\n- Honor `opts.replayReasoning`, which was ignored: thinking blocks always\n  became native reasoning parts. Off, they fold to labeled text.\n\nRobustness:\n- Import is not atomic — a rejected payload leaves a truncated session in the\n  DB. Delete it, and raise FabricationUnsupportedError so resume falls back to\n  bootstrap instead of surfacing a raw throw.\n- Record lineage against the id opencode actually stored.\n\nRemove the opencode shim. It triggered on `$# -eq 2`, so it intercepted\n`opencode -s <id>`, discarded the id, and re-entered itself through PATH —\nan infinite loop — while the bare form it documented passed through. opencode\nhas no argument-free \"show me my sessions\" invocation to interpose on.\n\nAlso: docs/specs/opencode-session-format.md with the evidence and the\nunknowns, an opencode row in the drift check (`opencode-ai`), opencode in the\ninteractive smoke test (which deletes its own session, since fabrication\nmutates a shared DB), and payload-shape tests covering each defect above.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RSV6y7vfeVapvuhimD3XmQ\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -2","description":"Commit the fixes"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"diagnostics":null,"id":"msg_011CdevkS8nbfgyur56KY3qU","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":426,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":426,"cache_read_input_tokens":175185,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":2,"iterations":[{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":426,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":426,"cache_read_input_tokens":175185,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1036,"type":"message"}],"output_tokens":1036,"server_tool_use":{"web_fetch_requests":0,"web_search_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"}},"parentUuid":"c1d948fc-fc1c-499d-8ab6-d969632c6517","requestId":"req_011CdevkQR6jbPaKL5iBDjnN","sessionId":"f6bb2ded-a3cb-4342-afd7-bbadf34f59ee","sessionKind":"bg","session_id":"f6bb2ded-a3cb-4342-afd7-bbadf34f59ee","timestamp":"2026-08-03T01:13:34.190Z","type":"assistant","userType":"external","uuid":"08608164-788a-4299-b596-a65dee100c41","version":"2.1.220"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-03T01:14:33.674Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
